Subject: [PATCH] Ayaneo Pocket DS buttons: the system only tells PocketDS Extra which button was pressed

The swap, AYA, home, profile and FPS buttons each sent their own broadcast (the swap did its job
in the system). They now all send org.lineageos.pocketds.parts.BUTTON with the name of the button
(swap, aya, home, profile, fps); PocketDS Extra decides what the button does, the user can change
it in the Controller page. The long press of the swap button (controller to the other screen) is
unchanged.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
@@ -4815,13 +4815,21 @@
             default:
                 action = null;
         }
+        // The long press of the swap button keeps its own broadcast. Every other press tells
+        // PocketDS Extra which button it was: the user chooses there what each button does (the
+        // defaults are the former actions), so the system has no list of actions to keep up.
+        final String button;
+        switch (code) {
+            case POCKETDS_KEY_SWAP: button = "swap"; break;
+            case POCKETDS_KEY_OVERLAY: button = "aya"; break;
+            case POCKETDS_KEY_HOME: button = "home"; break;
+            case POCKETDS_KEY_PROFILE: button = "profile"; break;
+            default: button = "fps"; break;
+        }
         mHandler.post(() -> {
-            if (action == null) {
-                togglePocketDsSwap();
-            } else {
-                mContext.sendBroadcastAsUser(new Intent(action).setPackage(POCKETDS_PACKAGE),
-                        UserHandle.CURRENT);
-            }
+            final Intent intent = held && action != null ? new Intent(action)
+                    : new Intent("org.lineageos.pocketds.parts.BUTTON").putExtra("button", button);
+            mContext.sendBroadcastAsUser(intent.setPackage(POCKETDS_PACKAGE), UserHandle.CURRENT);
         });
         return true;
     }
